    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Logistic-SuSiE approximations: the 022 protocol on a Gaussian and on a nested design\"\nsubtitle: \"CAVI-Q2 vs gIBSS-Q2 vs gIBSS-Laplace vs global-JJ vs score (experiments 023 and 024, L=5, 200 reps)\"\nengine: jupyter\njupyter: python3\nexecute:\n  fig-dpi: 110\n---\n\n\nTwo analogs of the [022 full grid](full_grid.qmd). The protocol is 022's: $p = 256$,\n$b_0 = -2$, $L^* = 3$ equal causals at gap 8 (correlated) or 64 (independent), fit with\n$L = 5$, EB prior variance, the same five arms in $\\mathcal{Q}_2$, 200 replicates per cell.\nOnly the design and its sweep change.\n\n- **023, Gaussian.** AR(1) Gaussian columns, $n = 500$, adjacent $\\rho = 0.9$ (causal-causal\n  latent correlation $0.9^8 = 0.43$ at gap 8, $\\approx 0$ at gap 64). Every column is dense and\n  $N(0, 1)$, so there is no set-size axis; the sweep is the signal $T = E[\\text{LRT}]$ per\n  causal in $\\{4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24\\}$, with one $\\beta$ per $T$. The dense control for 022's\n  sparse-set findings.\n- **024, nested.** `binary_attrition_X`: Markov roots (phi 0.8, half the rows) expanded into 32\n  blocks of 8 nested sets, each step keeping 55% of the parent's members, so one matrix holds\n  sets from 500 members down to 8. $n = 1000$. The sweep is the causals' depth $d \\in 0..7$,\n  i.e. their expected size $500 \\cdot 0.55^d$ (022's $m$), with $\\beta$ per $(d, T)$ and\n  $T \\in \\{8, 16\\}$. Causals sit at the same depth in blocks gap/8 apart; their decoys are\n  their own ancestors and descendants at other sizes.\n\nAll CS metrics are over **declared** CSs (component $\\log \\text{BF} \\ge 2$), as in 022.\n\n::: {#status .cell execution_count=2}\n- `023-laplace-gaussian`: 12 signal cells x 5 arms, 200-200 reps per cell; 200 null reps per arm.\n- `024-laplace-nested`: 32 signal cells x 5 arms, 200-200 reps per cell; 200 null reps per arm.\n:::\n\n\n# 023: Gaussian design, signal axis {#sec-gauss}\n\n## Headline: per gap, pooled over T {#sec-gauss-pooled}\n